## Overview

This Power BI dashboard was built for **TechNovaInc** to deliver a comprehensive, interactive view of sales performance. It surfaces key business metrics across regions, product categories, sales representatives, and time periods — with a country slicer enabling on-the-fly filtering across all visuals simultaneously.

---

## KPI Summary

Five headline metrics anchor the dashboard:

| KPI | Value |
|---|---|
| Total Revenue | 263.47K |
| Total Orders | 500 |
| Sum of Profit | 4.59K |
| Avg % of Discount | 15.18% |
| Net Revenue | 217.82K |

---

## Net Revenue by Region

A donut chart breaks down net revenue geographically. Revenue is distributed relatively evenly across five regions:

- **Asia**: 22.41%
- **North America**: 20.47%
- **South America**: 19.43%
- **Africa**: 19.3%
- **Europe**: 18.33%

The balanced distribution indicates a **global customer base** with no single region dominating, which has implications for currency risk and regional marketing spend.

---

## Gross Revenue by Category

A bar chart ranks product categories by gross revenue. **Accessories** and **Automotive** lead (~30–32K each), followed by Finance, Energy, Healthcare, Agriculture, Education, Travel, Electronics, and Construction. This ranking directly informs inventory prioritisation and category-level marketing investment decisions.

---

## Profit by Year & Sales Channel

A line chart reveals profit volatility from 2016–2024:

- Peak profit in **2018** (6K)
- Losses in **2020** and **2022** (both ~-2K) — likely COVID-era disruption
- Recovery to 4K in **2024**

The sales channel donut shows **online dominates at 82.7%** vs 17.3% offline — highlighting the importance of digital channel investment and optimisation.

---

## Sales & Profit by Representatives

A combo chart (bars = sales, line = profit) reveals important variance across the sales team:

- **Alice** and **Charlie** achieve the highest sales (~55–57K)
- **Diana** records **negative profit (-3.2K)** despite moderate sales (~47K) — suggesting excessive discounting or high cost-of-sale requiring management attention
- **Bob** has the lowest sales (47K) but positive profit (0.9K), indicating disciplined pricing

---

## Key Business Insights

1. **Diana's profit deficit** is the most actionable finding — discount policy review needed
2. **Online channel dominance** (82.7%) warrants continued digital investment
3. **2020/2022 loss years** suggest vulnerability to external shocks — scenario planning recommended
4. **Accessories & Automotive** are the highest-revenue categories — prime targets for upsell campaigns

---

## Conclusion

The Power BI dashboard enables TechNovaInc management to **drill into performance at a glance** — reducing time-to-insight from hours of spreadsheet analysis to seconds of interactive filtering. The country slicer adds another layer of analytical depth for regional management teams.

> **Tools used:** Power BI Desktop, DAX measures, custom donut/bar/combo/scatter charts, country-level slicer